      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

      <h3>Can children and seniors visit a luxury desert camp?</h3>
      <p>
        Yes. Because our luxury camps offer 4x4 dune transfers directly to the tent entrance, guests who prefer not to ride camels can easily arrive in comfort. Private bathrooms and real beds make the experience suitable for multi-generational families and travelers of all ages.
      </p>

      <h3>Is there mobile phone reception and Wi-Fi in the dunes?</h3>
      <p>
        Most top camps have 4G cellular coverage via Maroc Telecom, and several feature satellite Wi-Fi in the main dining tent. However, signals can fluctuate depending on dune topography and wind conditions. We encourage travelers to embrace the remote environment and disconnect for the night.
      </p>

      <h3>Can I take a private 4x4 instead of riding a camel?</h3>
      <p>
        Yes. Every guest has the choice between a camel caravan trek across the dune ridges or a direct private 4x4 transfer across the sand tracks. If you have mobility concerns or simply prefer vehicles, your chauffeur will drive you straight to camp.
      </p>

